**Data Structures:** Review the responsibilities of the classes to ensure they follow SRP (Single Responsibility Principle). It might be beneficial to separate data management (like reading/writing to files) from business logic. A new class, for example, `DataStorage`, could manage all file read/write operations, ensuring the `BMI_Calculator` class remains focused on BMI calculations only.

In summary, while the BMI Calculator project showcases a solid foundational implementation, several enhancements could be made regarding user input validation, UI clarity, data organization, and class responsibilities. These suggestions aim to improve the overall functionality while maintaining the simplicity and focus appropriate for a small project.

